msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-dump-path.md:16
msgid "To get a NAR containing the GNU Hello package:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-dump-path.md:22
msgid "To get a NAR from the binary cache https://cache.nixos.org/:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-dump-path.md:24
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix store dump-path --store https://cache.nixos.org/ \\\n"
"    /nix/store/vyrnv99qi410q82qp7nw7lcl37zmzaxd-glibc-2.25 > glibc.nar\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-dump-path.md:29
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-dump-path.md:31
msgid ""
"This command generates a [Nix Archive (NAR)](../../store/file-system-object/"
"content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) file containing the serialisation of "
"the store path [_installable_](./nix.md#installables). The NAR is written to "
"standard output."
msgstr ""

